# nl-memory-2: the maintenance actions of the `memory` tool (cycle1, flush, rebuild, backfill, manage, prune, purge, search, dump_session_roots)

New file (no module line needed, it is declared in service.rs): native/core/crates/mixdog-services/src/memory/service/maintenance.rs
The actions that need cycle1, the embedding flusher or the transcript ingest run through `Maintenance`, which the stack attaches.
Until it is attached they answer "memory maintenance is not available in this process"; prune, purge, search, dump_session_roots, status and core need only the database.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-services/src/memory/boot.rs, MemoryStack::start_with, inside Arc::new_cyclic

(a) Before the `let cycles = match cycles {` block, keep the memory section reader the cycles are built with:

    let cycle_config = cycles.as_ref().map(|cycles| cycles.config.clone());
    let projects_root = watch.as_ref().map(|watch| watch.projects_root.clone());

(b) After `let cycles = match cycles { ... };` (the CycleScheduler is Clone) and before `Self { ... }`:

    memory.attach_maintenance(crate::memory::service::maintenance::Maintenance::new(
        cycles.clone().zip(cycle_config),
        embed_flush.clone(),
        transcripts.clone(),
        projects_root,
        maintenance,
        lane,
    ));

`maintenance` (MaintenanceIo) and `lane` (DurabilityIo) are Copy and still in scope there; `watch` is moved into `Self` afterwards, so (a) reads it first.

## 2. Cargo
No dependency edge: mixdog-services already depends on futures, mixdog-rt, mixdog-statefile, tokio-util, chrono.

## 3. Protocol rows, SERVICE_PENDING
None: memory/memoryControl is already registered; its `args.action` now accepts the actions above.

## 4. Not wired here
The memory daemon's HTTP routes and <data>/channels/status-snapshot.json are not ported; see the task result.
